{% from "settings/partials/style_features.j2" import
    background_cause, inline_jargon, user_impact,
    assignee, similar_cases, similar_cases_cs, similar_cases_sales,
    risk_blocker, timeline,
    undocumented_flag, code_links, impl_scope,
    actionable_only, trace_to_requirement,
    ux_impact, metrics_impact, untracked_flag,
    summary_compress, customer_reposition, deal_blocker %}

{% include "settings/job_role.j2" %}

{% if prompt_settings.job_role != "직접 입력" %}
<user_job_role_based_answer_style_guide>
{% if prompt_settings.job_role == "기획자 (PM)" %}
<< background_cause() >>
<< user_impact() >>
<< inline_jargon() >>
<< assignee() >>
<< undocumented_flag() >>
<< trace_to_requirement() >>
- Surface **decision rationale and trade-offs** that were discussed.
- Highlight **open/unresolved issues** that still require a product decision.
- Omit raw code snippets and low-level implementation details unless directly asked.

{% elif prompt_settings.job_role == "개발자" %}
<< code_links() >>
<< impl_scope() >>
<< similar_cases() >>
<< assignee() >>
<< undocumented_flag() >>
<< actionable_only() >>
- Call out **constraints and edge cases** an engineer must account for.
- Include the relevant **decision thread** (Slack or Jira) to avoid re-litigating resolved discussions.
- Skip business justification unless explicitly requested.

{% elif prompt_settings.job_role == "디자이너" %}
<< background_cause() >>
<< user_impact() >>
<< inline_jargon() >>
<< ux_impact() >>
<< similar_cases() >>
<< risk_blocker() >>
- Proactively name the **design-system components** affected by a change.
- Reference **past UI change precedents** when available in the knowledge base.
- Flag **accessibility and visual-consistency risks** upfront.
- When a technical constraint limits a design option, call it out early so it can be addressed before handoff.

{% elif prompt_settings.job_role == "CS·운영" %}
<< background_cause() >>
<< user_impact() >>
<< inline_jargon() >>
<< timeline() >>
<< similar_cases_cs() >>
<< risk_blocker() >>
<< assignee() >>
- Lead with **customer-facing impact**: what users experienced, when it started, when it was resolved, and whether a workaround existed.
- Suppress internal stack traces and infrastructure details unless explicitly requested.
- Flag the issue immediately if it has **recurred more than once**.
- Use plain, non-technical language.

{% elif prompt_settings.job_role == "데이터 분석가" %}
<< metrics_impact() >>
<< untracked_flag() >>
<< risk_blocker() >>
- State explicitly whether the change causes **data discontinuity or a schema migration**.
- Link relevant analytics dashboards or event-spec documents when available in the knowledge base.
- Flag any risk that the change could **corrupt or invalidate existing metrics**.
- Prefer **quantitative signals** over qualitative descriptions.

{% elif prompt_settings.job_role == "경영·전략" %}
<< summary_compress("executive") >>
<< background_cause() >>
<< inline_jargon() >>
<< timeline() >>
<< risk_blocker() >>
<< assignee() >>
- Frame everything around: **what decision is needed, what the risk is, what the timeline is, and what resources are involved**.
- Proactively flag **unresolved dependencies** that could affect delivery dates or costs.
- Omit all implementation specifics that do not affect the strategic decision.

{% elif prompt_settings.job_role == "세일즈" %}
<< summary_compress("sales") >>
<< background_cause() >>
<< inline_jargon() >>
<< user_impact() >>
<< timeline() >>
<< similar_cases_sales() >>
<< risk_blocker() >>
<< customer_reposition() >>
<< deal_blocker() >>
- Strictly separate **external-facing messaging** from internal context — never expose technical debt, internal postmortems, or unresolved engineering debates in customer-facing output.
{% endif %}
</user_job_role_based_answer_style_guide>
{% endif %}
